From c24b360ce80f58bda24e56d0f2b80ebbaacda91a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:58:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] emacs: git without advice -- speculation, stdin/env,
 async over git.spawn

- no magit function is advised or redefined: git reaches the agent via
  the process-file / start-file-process file-name-handler operations
- read-only batches are predicted from the previous run of the same
  command and sent at once; a status refresh is one round trip
- stdin and environment are carried (hunk staging, GIT_INDEX_FILE)
- asynchronous git (apply, commit with with-editor, rebase, push...) is
  a real local process object bridged to git.spawn
- eglot: tunnel writes are coalesced
- docs

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
